# Model reminder before coding

The user is training a habit: pick the model that matches the work, not the most expensive one every time. They use their own Anthropic key so Cursor quota is not the limit.

**Before writing or changing code, config that affects trading, or tests,** start the reply with a short model reminder. Do not start coding in the same breath if they should switch. One or two lines is enough.

| Work | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Everyday building: tests, Telegram, docs, refactors, plumbing | Claude Sonnet, ~200k context, medium effort |
| Money decisions: entries, exits, risk, sizing, allocation, backtester design, paper-run or backtest review | Claude Opus, ~200k context, high effort if they want extra care |
| A single chat that is actually full (rare; they usually start a new chat per topic) | Turn on 1M context |
| Isolated mechanical code with no judgment | DeepSeek is optional and cheap. Do not use it as the main model for this project. |

Do not recommend Opus 5.5 with 1M and high effort as the default. That combination is overkill here.

Skip the reminder on pure discussion, questions, or reviews with no code change. If the work already matches the model they are likely on, a one-line confirmation is enough. You cannot switch their model picker; tell them what to select.
